note right of Store
  Unique:
  slug

  baseCurrency is the main reporting/accounting currency of the store.
  All *Base monetary fields are stored in this currency.

  costingMethod defines how cost of goods is calculated.
  Recommended default for MVP: average_cost.
  FIFO can be enabled later using WarehouseStockBatch
  and batch-level StockMovement records.

  allowBackorders=true means OrderEntry can be created
  even when there is no available stock yet.
  Reservation and shipment still cannot exceed available physical stock.
end note



note right of Currency
  code uses ISO 4217-like values: UAH, USD, EUR.
  Currency is a dictionary, not a per-store entity.
end note

note right of ExchangeRate
  rate means: 1 fromCurrency = rate toCurrency.
  Recommended use: document currency -> Store.baseCurrency.

  Store can override rates manually for accounting needs.
  If store is null, the rate can be treated as a global/reference rate.

  Keep the rate snapshot on documents too, because historical
  documents must not change when ExchangeRate is edited later.
end note

note right of User
  Unique:
  nickname
  email
end note

note right of UserStore
  Primary key:
  (user_id, store_id)
end note

note right of Category
  Unique:
  (store_id, parent_id, name) when parent_id is not null
  (store_id, name) when parent_id is null
end note

note right of CategoryAdditionalName
  Unique:
  (store_id, additional_name_id, category_id)
end note

note right of CategoryProductParameterName
  Unique:
  (category_id, product_parameter_name_id)
end note

note right of Product
  Unique:
  (store_id, code)

  unit is a reference to Unit to avoid inconsistent text values like:
  шт, шт., штук, pcs.

  baseSalePrice is recommended to be stored in Store.baseCurrency.
  It is a denormalized quick access value for the current regular sale price.
  ProductPrice stores price history and special price types.
end note


note right of Product
  Product is used as a universal stock/catalog item:
  - material: purchased and consumed in production
  - finished_product: manufactured and sold
  - resale_product: purchased and sold without manufacturing
  - semi_finished_product: produced and later consumed/finished
  - service: can be sold, but usually should not create WarehouseStock movements

  Recommended flag rules:
  material: canBePurchased=true, canBeSold=false, canBeManufactured=false
  finished_product: canBeSold=true, canBeManufactured=true
  resale_product: canBePurchased=true, canBeSold=true, canBeManufactured=false
  semi_finished_product: canBeManufactured=true and canBePurchased/canBeSold depends on business case
  service: canBeSold=true, but should normally not be stocked

  Avoid splitting Product/Material/Item at this stage.
  Use productKind + flags to control behavior in forms and business rules.
end note

note right of ProductPrice
  Product price history and future price support.

  price is in ProductPrice.currency.
  priceBase is in Store.baseCurrency using the exchange rate at creation/update time.

  Suggested rules:
  - regular = default catalog price
  - sale = promotional price
  - wholesale = wholesale price
  - custom = manual/special price list

  Only one active price interval should overlap for the same:
  (store_id, product_id, type, currency_id).

  OrderEntry.unitPrice remains the final price snapshot used in a specific order.
end note

note right of Unit
  Unique:
  (store_id, code)

  precision defines how many decimal places are allowed for this unit.
  Examples:
  шт -> 0
  кг -> 3
  м -> 3
  м2 -> 3
end note

note right of Customer
  Unique suggestion:
  (store_id, phone) where phone is not null
  (store_id, email) where email is not null

  Order keeps customer snapshots so old orders do not change
  after editing Customer data.
end note

note right of Supplier
  Unique suggestion:
  (store_id, name)

  Purchase keeps supplier snapshots so old purchase documents do not change
  after editing Supplier data.
end note

note right of ProductParameter
  Unique:
  (product_id, product_parameter_name_id)
end note

note right of Warehouse
  Unique:
  (store_id, name)
end note

note right of WarehouseStock
  Unique:
  (product_id, warehouse_id)

  quantityOnHand and averageCost should be updated only through posted StockMovement records.
  reservedQuantity can be stored for speed or calculated from active StockReservation rows.
  availableQuantity should be calculated as quantityOnHand - reservedQuantity.
end note

note right of WarehouseStockBatch
  Batch belongs to WarehouseStock, so product and warehouse are derived from WarehouseStock.
  purchaseEntry is optional because batches can be created by purchase, production, return, adjustment, or initial stock.
  Prefer createdByMovement as the universal source of a created batch.
  unitCost is stored in Store.baseCurrency. Original supplier currency is kept in Purchase/PurchaseEntry.
end note

note right of Order
  Customer is optional to allow quick one-time orders.
  createdBy/updatedBy/canceledBy are audit fields for admin accountability.
  canceledAt should be filled when status becomes canceled.
  customerNameSnapshot/customerPhoneSnapshot/customerEmailSnapshot store contact data at order time.

  currency stores the original sale currency.
  exchangeRateToBase is a snapshot: 1 order currency = X Store.baseCurrency.
  totalAmount is in original currency; totalAmountBase is in Store.baseCurrency.
end note

note right of Purchase
  Supplier is optional to allow quick/manual purchases.
  createdBy/updatedBy/canceledBy are audit fields for admin accountability.
  canceledAt should be filled when status becomes canceled.
  supplierNameSnapshot/supplierPhoneSnapshot/supplierEmailSnapshot store supplier data at purchase time.

  currency stores the original purchase currency.
  exchangeRateToBase is a snapshot: 1 purchase currency = X Store.baseCurrency.
  totalAmount/deliveryCost are in original currency; *Base fields are in Store.baseCurrency.
end note


note right of OrderStatus
  Recommended order flow:
  draft -> confirmed -> awaiting_stock -> ready_to_ship -> partially_shipped -> shipped -> delivered -> completed.

  canceled is for orders stopped before completion.
  partially_returned/returned are post-shipment states.
  Backorders usually use awaiting_stock until enough stock is produced, purchased or reserved.
end note

note right of PurchaseStatus
  Recommended purchase flow:
  draft -> ordered -> partially_received -> received -> completed.

  partially_returned/returned are used when goods are returned to supplier.
  canceled is for purchases stopped before they are completed.
end note

note right of InventoryDocumentStatus
  draft = editable document, no stock effect.
  posted = immutable document; stock movements were created.
  canceled = document was canceled through reversal logic or became inactive by business flow.

  Avoid editing posted documents directly.
end note

note right of ProductionOrderStatus
  Recommended production flow:
  draft -> planned -> materials_reserved -> in_progress -> completed.

  materials_reserved means required stock was reserved but production has not started yet.
  Actual material consumption happens through InventoryDocument(type=production) OUT lines.
end note


note right of Payment
  Universal payment table for customer payments and supplier payments.

  Direction:
  - incoming: money received, usually for Order.
  - outgoing: money paid, usually for Purchase.

  Rules:
  - exactly one of order or purchase should be filled.
  - Order payments are usually incoming.
  - Purchase payments are usually outgoing.
  - refunds can use type=refund with the opposite direction.
  - amount is in payment currency.
  - amountBase is stored in Store.baseCurrency using exchangeRateToBase snapshot.

  Do not rely only on Order.paidAt for payment state.
  Payment records are the source of truth for paid/remaining amounts.
end note

note right of OrderEntry
  Sales order line.
  Stores snapshot of product name, code, unit code/name, quantity and sale price at the moment of order.
  Monetary fields without Base suffix are in Order.currency. Base fields are in Store.baseCurrency.

  shippedQuantity, returnedQuantity and canceledQuantity are denormalized progress/cache fields
  for fast UI and filtering. Source of truth is InventoryDocumentLine + posted StockMovement.
  If cache becomes inconsistent, recalculate it from posted inventory documents.

  Partial shipments are allowed:
  one OrderEntry can be linked to multiple InventoryDocumentLine rows over time.
  Backordered quantity = quantity - shippedQuantity - canceledQuantity, with reservations handled separately.

  InventoryDocumentLine is created from this line when stock is shipped or returned.
end note

note right of PurchaseEntry
  Purchase line.
  Stores snapshot of product name, code, unit code/name, quantity, unit cost, delivery cost and optional planned sale price.
  Monetary fields without Base suffix are in Purchase.currency. Base fields are in Store.baseCurrency.

  receivedQuantity and returnedQuantity are denormalized progress/cache fields
  for fast UI and filtering. Source of truth is InventoryDocumentLine + posted StockMovement.
  If cache becomes inconsistent, recalculate it from posted inventory documents.

  Partial receipts are allowed:
  one PurchaseEntry can be linked to multiple InventoryDocumentLine rows over time.
  Open quantity = quantity - receivedQuantity + returnedQuantity, depending on final business rules.

  InventoryDocumentLine and WarehouseStockBatch are created when purchase is posted/received.
end note

note right of InventoryDocument
  createdBy/updatedBy/postedBy/canceledBy are audit fields.
  postedBy should be filled when status becomes posted; canceledBy should be filled when status becomes canceled.

  Unique:
  (store_id, number)

  Check constraint:
  only one of order_id, purchase_id, production_order_id can be not null.

  currency/exchangeRateToBase are optional because purely technical documents
  like stock_adjustment may not have external monetary currency.
  If present, amount fields without Base suffix are in document currency; Base fields are in Store.baseCurrency.

  reason is optional, but recommended for write_off, stock_adjustment,
  production_loss, return and inventory_count scenarios.

  Inventory count MVP approach:
  do not create separate StockCount/StockCountLine tables yet.
  Use InventoryDocument(type=stock_adjustment) with InventoryReason(type=inventory_count).
  InventoryDocumentLine.quantity stores the adjustment difference, not the counted total.
  Example: system has 10, counted 8 => OUT line quantity 2.
  Direct editing of WarehouseStock quantities should be avoided.

  This is the main inventory operation document.
  It replaces polymorphic source_type/source_id for stock logic.

  Posted documents should not be edited directly.
  Cancellation should create reversal document/movements instead of deleting original movements.

  Only reversal documents should have reversedDocument filled.
  reversedDocument points to the original posted document being canceled/reversed.
  Do not add separate reversalDocument column; reverse lookup can be done by query or ORM mappedBy.
end note

note right of InventoryReason
  Dictionary of reasons for inventory documents.
  Useful for analytics and consistent grouping of write-offs,
  stock adjustments, production losses, returns and inventory counts.

  Unique suggestion:
  (store_id, type, name)

  Examples:
  Брак, пошкодження, обрізки, інвентаризація, пересорт,
  стартові залишки, повернення клієнта.
end note


note right of StatusHistory
  Universal status history table for main business documents:
  Order, Purchase, InventoryDocument, ProductionOrder.

  Uses entityType + entityId intentionally for MVP flexibility.
  Important limitation: database cannot enforce foreign key to different tables.
  Application code must validate that entityId exists for the selected entityType.

  Suggested rule:
  create a StatusHistory row every time document status changes.
end note

note right of InventoryDocumentLine
  One posted line creates one or more StockMovement records.
  Monetary fields without Base suffix follow InventoryDocument.currency.
  Base fields are in Store.baseCurrency.

  Partial operations are represented by multiple lines/documents over time:
  - one OrderEntry can have several sale_shipment/customer_return lines
  - one PurchaseEntry can have several purchase_receipt/supplier_return lines
  OrderEntry/PurchaseEntry progress fields are cache, not the main source of truth.

  For production documents use:
  - OUT lines for consumed materials
  - IN lines for produced goods

  For transfer documents use paired lines:
  - OUT from source warehouse
  - IN into destination warehouse
end note

note right of StockMovement
  quantityChange is signed:
  positive = stock increase
  negative = stock decrease

  Use warehouseStockBatch for FIFO/batch-level costing when needed.
  StockMovement.unitCost is always stored in Store.baseCurrency.
  For average_cost method, StockMovement.unitCost stores the cost snapshot used for this movement.

  In average_cost mode, OUT movement unitCost usually equals WarehouseStock.averageCost at posting time.
  In fifo mode, one InventoryDocumentLine may create multiple StockMovement rows for different batches.
end note

note right of StockReservation
  Used when an order reserves stock before shipment.
  WarehouseStock.reservedQuantity can be calculated from active reservations.
end note


note right of Payment
  Payment records are the source of truth for financial payments.

  Order.paidAmountBase / Purchase.paidAmountBase and paymentStatus are denormalized cache fields
  for fast lists, filters, and dashboards.

  They should be recalculated from Payment rows after creating, updating, deleting, or reversing payments.
  paidAt can store the date when the document became fully paid.
end note

note right of ProductionRecipe
  Describes bill of materials for manufactured products.
end note

note right of ProductionRecipeItem
  material is also Product, but with canBePurchased=true
  and usually canBeSold=false.
end note

note right of ProductionOrderMaterial
  Planned material list for a specific ProductionOrder.
  Usually copied from ProductionRecipeItem at the moment production is created.

  This preserves the plan even if the recipe changes later.
  Actual consumption is recorded by InventoryDocumentLine(direction=out).
  Plan/fact comparison:
  ProductionOrderMaterial.plannedQuantity vs actual OUT InventoryDocumentLine quantity.
end note

note right of ProductionOrder
  ProductionOrder plans manufacturing.
  createdBy/updatedBy/startedBy/completedBy/canceledBy are audit fields for production accountability.
  canceledAt should be filled when status becomes canceled.
  recipe is optional, because production can be based on a recipe or created manually.

  ProductionOrderMaterial stores the planned material snapshot for this exact order.
  InventoryDocument(type=production) posts actual stock movements.
end note


note bottom
  Final cleanup decisions:
  - ExchangeRate is a financial/reference entity and should not depend on InventoryReason.
  - Batch-level stock attribution should be handled through StockMovement.warehouseStockBatch, not directly from InventoryDocumentLine.
  - canceledAt is stored on Order, Purchase and ProductionOrder together with canceledBy.
  - Payment has updatedBy because payment records can be corrected while still preserving audit information.
  - Keep technical stock tables controlled by posting/canceling documents, not by manual admin edits.
end note

note bottom
  Database constraints / invariants to implement in migrations and services:

  Global numeric rules:
  - All quantity fields must be >= 0, except StockMovement.quantityChange which can be positive or negative.
  - InventoryDocumentLine.quantity > 0. Direction defines IN/OUT, not the sign.
  - StockMovement.quantityChange != 0.
  - Monetary amount fields should be >= 0 unless a special reversal/discount rule explicitly allows otherwise.
  - Currency exchangeRateToBase > 0 when currency is present.

  WarehouseStock:
  - unique(store_id via warehouse, warehouse_id, product_id).
  - quantityOnHand >= 0.
  - reservedQuantity >= 0.
  - reservedQuantity <= quantityOnHand.
  - Backorders are allowed at OrderEntry level only; WarehouseStock must never go negative.
  - averageCost >= 0.
  - Product with productKind=service should not create WarehouseStock or StockMovement rows.

  WarehouseStockBatch:
  - initialQuantity > 0.
  - remainingQuantity >= 0.
  - remainingQuantity <= initialQuantity.
  - unitCost >= 0.
  - createdByMovement should normally reference an IN StockMovement.

  InventoryDocument:
  - unique(store_id, number).
  - createdBy should be filled when document is created by authenticated user.
  - postedBy is required when status=posted.
  - canceledBy is required when status=canceled.
  - only one of order_id, purchase_id, production_order_id can be not null.
  - postedAt is required when status=posted.
  - canceledAt is required when status=canceled.
  - Only type=reversal should have reversedDocument filled.
  - reversedDocument must point to a posted document.
  - A document should not reverse itself.
  - Posted documents are immutable; corrections are done by reversal documents.

  InventoryDocumentLine:
  - product.store must match inventoryDocument.store.
  - warehouse.store must match inventoryDocument.store.
  - warehouseStock, when filled, must match line product + warehouse.
  - For sale_shipment lines, direction should be out.
  - For purchase_receipt lines, direction should be in.
  - For customer_return lines, direction should be in.
  - For supplier_return lines, direction should be out.
  - For transfer documents, lines should be paired: one OUT and one IN for the same product and quantity.

  StockMovement:
  - Must be created only from posted InventoryDocumentLine.
  - quantityChange sign must match line direction: IN > 0, OUT < 0.
  - warehouseStock must match the InventoryDocumentLine product and warehouse.
  - OUT movement must not make WarehouseStock.quantityOnHand negative.
  - In FIFO mode, OUT movements using batches must not exceed WarehouseStockBatch.remainingQuantity.

  StockReservation:
  - quantity > 0.
  - active reservations must not exceed available stock: quantityOnHand - reservedQuantity.
  - Backordered OrderEntry rows should remain unreserved until stock is available.
  - completed/canceled/expired reservations should not be counted in WarehouseStock.reservedQuantity.

  OrderEntry / PurchaseEntry:
  - quantity > 0.
  - OrderEntry can exist without stock when Store.allowBackorders=true.
  - OrderEntry without stock must not automatically create StockReservation or StockMovement.
  - progress quantities must be >= 0.
  - shippedQuantity, returnedQuantity, canceledQuantity, receivedQuantity are denormalized cache fields.
  - Source of truth for progress is posted InventoryDocumentLine + StockMovement.
  - Recalculate progress cache after posting/canceling/reversing inventory documents.
  - shippedQuantity should not exceed OrderEntry.quantity - canceledQuantity.
  - returnedQuantity should not exceed shippedQuantity.
  - receivedQuantity should not exceed PurchaseEntry.quantity.
  - PurchaseEntry.returnedQuantity should not exceed receivedQuantity.
  - Snapshot fields should be filled at creation and not overwritten automatically when Product changes.

  Payment:
  - amount > 0.
  - amountBase > 0.
  - exchangeRateToBase > 0.
  - exactly one of order_id or purchase_id should be filled.
  - incoming payments usually belong to Order; outgoing payments usually belong to Purchase.
  - refund payments may intentionally use the opposite direction.
  - Order/Purchase paidAmountBase and paymentStatus are cache fields.
  - Source of truth is sum(Payment.amountBase) against document totalAmountBase.
  - unpaid: paidAmountBase = 0.
  - partially_paid: 0 < paidAmountBase < totalAmountBase.
  - paid: paidAmountBase = totalAmountBase.
  - overpaid: paidAmountBase > totalAmountBase.
  - refunded: use when effective paid amount returns to 0 after refund, if business rules require a separate visible state.

  ProductPrice / ExchangeRate:
  - ProductPrice valid intervals should not overlap for the same store + product + type + currency.
  - ExchangeRate valid intervals should not overlap for the same store/global + fromCurrency + toCurrency.
  - fromCurrency and toCurrency should be different, unless explicitly storing rate=1 for the same currency.

  Deletion / archiving policy:
  - Business documents should not be physically deleted: Order, Purchase, InventoryDocument, Payment, ProductionOrder.
  - Stock history should not be physically deleted: InventoryDocumentLine, StockMovement, WarehouseStockBatch, StockReservation.
  - Reference data can be deactivated via status=inactive and hidden from creation forms.
  - Reference data can use deletedAt for soft delete only when it is not needed in active workflows.
  - Soft-deleted reference rows must remain readable from old documents and reports.
  - Product, Customer, Supplier, Warehouse, Unit, Category, InventoryReason and ProductPrice use soft-delete/archiving behavior.
  - Currency and ExchangeRate should normally be disabled/expired, not deleted, because old financial documents may depend on them.

  Cancellation timestamps:
  - Order.canceledAt should be filled when Order.status=canceled.
  - Purchase.canceledAt should be filled when Purchase.status=canceled.
  - ProductionOrder.canceledAt should be filled when ProductionOrder.status=canceled.

  Status transitions:
  - Order statuses should follow the recommended flow; do not jump to completed without delivered/shipped business confirmation.
  - Purchase statuses should follow draft -> ordered -> partially_received/received -> completed.
  - InventoryDocument can affect stock only when status=posted.
  - ProductionOrder can become in_progress only after materials are reserved or an explicit override is allowed.
  - Every status transition should create StatusHistory.

  Audit fields:
  - createdBy/updatedBy/postedBy/canceledBy/startedBy/completedBy should reference existing users.
  - Do not use these fields as permission model; they are historical audit data.
  - StatusHistory should still be created for each status transition.

  Production:
  - ProductionOrder.product should usually have canBeManufactured=true.
  - ProductionRecipe.product should usually have canBeManufactured=true.
  - ProductionRecipeItem.material and ProductionOrderMaterial.material should usually not be productKind=service.
  - Production actual material usage is recorded via InventoryDocumentLine OUT lines, not by editing ProductionOrderMaterial.
end note


